/// OTP supervisor restart strategy — how sibling children are affected when
/// one of them crashes.
type SupervisionStrategy = #oneForOne | #oneForAll | #restForOne
/// Supervisor — Abstract base class for static OTP supervision trees.
///
/// Subclass `Supervisor` to define a static supervision tree: one whose
/// children are known at startup. Override `childSpecs` to return the list
/// of child classes (or `SupervisionSpec` values for per-child
/// configuration). All other configuration methods have sensible defaults
/// that can be selectively overridden.
///
/// ## Configuration runs inside the supervisor's `init`
///
/// Configuration (`childSpecs`, `strategy`, `maxRestarts`, `restartWindow`)
/// is instance-side (ADR 0135 §2): the runtime sends each setting to the
/// supervisor being started, from inside its own OTP `init/1`. So `self` is
/// that supervisor and `self args` its start args (`nil` for `supervise`).
/// Two rules follow:
///
/// - **Do not send messages to `self`** from a configuration method
///   (`self count`, `self which: X`): the supervisor is still starting, and
///   the start fails with `#supervisor_start_failed`. Reading `self args` and
///   passing `self` *as a value* (e.g. in a child's args) are fine.
/// - **Do not send to the supervisor's own class** (`self class helper`,
///   `MySup settings`) from configuration while `supervise` is starting it:
///   `supervise` currently runs in that class's process (until BT-3962), so
///   the send waits on the busy class and times out. Pass values in through
///   start args, or nest the supervisor under another one.
/// - **Never synchronously call a supervisor from code it is waiting on**:
///   its configuration methods, those of its nested supervisor children, or
///   the `initialize` of a `withName:`/`withClassMethod:` actor child. A call
///   to an ancestor from there hangs during start, every OTP restart and
///   every `DynamicSupervisor startChild:`.
///
/// Each setting is a separate send, so put expensive work (reading files,
/// say) in `childSpecs` only.
///
/// See ADR 0059 and ADR 0135 for the full design.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// Supervisor subclass: WebApp
///   childSpecs => #(DatabasePool HTTPRouter MetricsCollector)
///
/// app := (WebApp supervise) unwrap
/// app count   // => 3
/// ```
///
/// @see DynamicSupervisor (for runtime-added children)
/// @see Actor (base class for supervised processes)
/// @see SupervisionSpec (for per-child configuration)
abstract Object subclass: Supervisor

  // === Class-side ===

  /// Whether this class is a supervisor (always true for Supervisor subclasses).
  ///
  /// Used by `SupervisionSpec childSpec` to determine `type` and `shutdown`.
  class isSupervisor -> Boolean => true

  // === Class-side lifecycle ===

  /// Start this supervisor (or return the already-running instance).
  ///
  /// Registers the supervisor under its class name. Subsequent calls to
  /// `supervise` or `current` return the running instance.
  ///
  /// ADR 0080 Phase 2 (BT-1999): returns `Result(Self, Error)` so subclass
  /// typing is preserved (e.g. `MySupervisor supervise unwrap` is typed as
  /// `MySupervisor`, not the abstract `Supervisor` base). Use `unwrap` for
  /// boot-style "crash on failure" call sites, or `ifOk:ifError:` /
  /// `andThen:` for recoverable starts. Failures surface as
  /// `Result error: #beamtalk_error{kind = supervisor_start_failed}`.
  class supervise -> Result(Self, Error) =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) startLink: self

  /// Return the running supervisor instance, or nil if not started.
  class current -> Self | Nil => (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) current: self

  // === Instance-side configuration (override in concrete subclasses) ===
  //
  // Read from the supervisor being started, inside its `init/1` (ADR 0135).

  /// Return the list of child classes (or SupervisionSpec values) for this supervisor.
  ///
  /// Must be overridden by concrete subclasses. Raises SubclassResponsibility otherwise.
  /// Runs inside the supervisor's own `init`: use `self args` for start args
  /// and pass `self` as a value if a child needs its parent, but do not send
  /// messages to `self` (see the class comment).
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// Supervisor subclass: WebApp
  ///   childSpecs => #(DatabasePool HTTPRouter)
  /// ```
  childSpecs -> List => self subclassResponsibility

  /// OTP supervisor restart strategy.
  ///
  /// Valid values: `#oneForOne`, `#oneForAll`, `#restForOne`.
  /// Default: `#oneForOne`.
  strategy -> SupervisionStrategy => #oneForOne

  /// Maximum number of restarts within `restartWindow` seconds.
  ///
  /// If this rate is exceeded, the supervisor itself shuts down.
  maxRestarts -> Integer => 10

  /// Time window in seconds for the `maxRestarts` rate limit.
  restartWindow -> Integer => 60

  /// The start args this supervisor was started with: `nil` for `supervise`.
  ///
  /// OTP restarts replay the same args, so a restarted supervisor recomputes
  /// the same configuration. Readable from the configuration methods (inside
  /// `init`) and from outside; raises with kind `#stale_handle` when the
  /// supervisor is no longer running.
  args -> Dynamic => self argsResult unwrap

  /// Internal FFI seam (ADR 0101 Part 4): the raw `Result`-shaped `args/1` call.
  internal argsResult => (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) args: self

  /// Lifecycle hook called after all children have started.
  ///
  /// Override to perform post-start wiring (e.g., discovering siblings
  /// via `which:` or injecting dependencies). `self` is the new supervisor.
  /// Runs in the caller's process after the supervisor has finished
  /// starting, so `which:` and other messages to `self` work here (unlike
  /// in the configuration methods). If it raises, the supervisor is stopped
  /// and the start fails.
  ///
  /// Fires exactly once, at the initial `supervise` call — it does
  /// **not** re-fire on OTP-driven child restarts (including
  /// `restForOne` cascades), since those start each child directly
  /// from its child spec and never re-enter this dispatch path. A
  /// dependency reference that must survive a restart needs named
  /// actor registration (see ADR 0079) instead of one-shot wiring here.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// Supervisor subclass: App
  ///   childSpecs => #(Store, Engine)
  ///   initialize =>
  ///     engine := (self which: Engine) unwrap
  ///     store := (self which: Store) unwrap
  ///     engine connectStore: store
  /// ```
  initialize -> Nil => nil

  // === Instance-side inspection ===

  /// Return the OTP child ids of currently-running children.
  ///
  /// BT-1997 / ADR 0080 Phase 1: `whichChildren/1` returns a Result-shaped
  /// value; call `unwrap` at the FFI boundary so the user-facing signature is
  /// a list of child-id Symbols while the runtime migrates to Result returns.
  /// Stdlib signature updates land in Phase 2 (BT-P2-stdlib).
  ///
  /// BT-2254: now that FFI list element types are carried, `whichChildren`'s
  /// `{ok, [atom()]}` spec resolves `unwrap` to `List(Symbol)`. The declared
  /// return type matches that inferred body type so no type-mismatch warning
  /// is produced (the runtime value is a list of atoms, i.e. `List(Symbol)`).
  children -> List(Symbol) => self whichChildrenResult unwrap

  /// Internal FFI seam (ADR 0101 Part 4): the raw `Result`-shaped
  /// `whichChildren/1` call. Keeps `children` pure Beamtalk.
  internal whichChildrenResult -> Result(List(Symbol), Error) =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) whichChildren: self

  /// Look up the running child process for the given class.
  ///
  /// ADR 0080 Phase 2 (BT-2041): returns `Result(Object, Error)`. The ok
  /// variant spans `Object | nil` — a class with no running child returns
  /// `Result ok: nil`, not an error. Genuine failures (e.g. supervisor
  /// process dead) surface as `Result error: #beamtalk_error{kind = stale_handle}`.
  which: aClass :: Class -> Result(Object, Error) =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) whichChild: self class: aClass

  /// Terminate the running child process for the given class.
  ///
  /// ADR 0080 Phase 2 (BT-1999): returns `Result(Nil, Error)`. Idempotent
  /// on `not_found` — terminating an already-gone child returns `Result ok: nil`.
  /// Genuine failures surface as
  /// `Result error: #beamtalk_error{kind = terminate_failed}`.
  terminate: aClass :: Class -> Result(Nil, Error) =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) terminateChild: self class: aClass

  /// Return the count of currently-running children.
  ///
  /// BT-1997 / ADR 0080 Phase 1: `countChildren/1` returns a Result-shaped
  /// value; call `unwrap` at the FFI boundary to preserve the pre-migration
  /// user-facing signature.
  count -> Integer => self countChildrenResult unwrap

  /// Internal FFI seam (ADR 0101 Part 4): the raw `Result`-shaped
  /// `countChildren/1` call. Keeps `count` pure Beamtalk.
  internal countChildrenResult -> Result(Integer, Error) =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) countChildren: self

  /// Stop this supervisor and all its children.
  ///
  /// BT-1997 / ADR 0080 Phase 1: `stop/1` returns a Result-shaped value;
  /// call `unwrap` at the FFI boundary to preserve the pre-migration
  /// user-facing signature.
  stop -> Nil => self stopResult unwrap

  /// Internal FFI seam (ADR 0101 Part 4): the raw `Result`-shaped `stop/1`
  /// call. Keeps `stop` pure Beamtalk.
  internal stopResult -> Result(Nil, Error) =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_supervisor) stop: self
